QUESTSHARE QUEST-SHARE QUESTSHARING

	g>Description:	n

Share an active quest with another player in your party. The recipient must
choose to accept before the quest is added to their list. Sharing does not
transfer your progress, remove your quest, or mark anything completed.

	g>Usage:	n

  quest progress
  quest share <index> <player>
  quest accept
  quest decline

Use quest progress to see your active quest indexes. For example:

  quest share 0 Caide

The recipient can then type quest accept or quest decline. Offers expire after
two minutes. A player can have only one pending offer at a time.

	g>Requirements:	n

Both characters must be players, connected, in the same party, and in the same
room. The sharing player must still have the quest active when it is accepted.

The recipient must qualify for the quest normally: meet its level limits,
complete required previous quests and dialogue branches, possess any required
object in inventory or equipment, and have a free quest slot. They cannot
already have the quest, or repeat a completed quest unless it is repeatable.
Shared quests do not receive staff eligibility overrides.

These requirements are checked when the offer is sent and again when accepted.
If the offer can no longer be accepted, request a new offer after resolving
the problem. An accepted quest begins with fresh progress and its full normal
time allowance, independently of the sharing player's progress and timer.

	g>Builder Notes:	n

The NO-SHARE quest flag in QEDIT prevents sharing. Existing quests remain
shareable unless this flag is set. Changing the flag also prevents acceptance
of an outstanding offer for that quest. The flag does not prevent normal
questmaster joining or change the separate rules for party objective credit.

	ySee also:	n QUEST, GROUP, QEDIT
